IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nrs-dates`
IMPORT `nrs-survivor`

-- Cases for the survivor's seat of the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (and the s 30(2) formula in the formulas sidecar)
-- before the run. Amounts of the form 20000 x 1.019^n were worked with exact decimals and rounded up to the cent:
-- 1.019^1 = 1.019, 1.019^2 = 1.038361, 1.019^3 = 1.058089859, 1.019^10 = 1.20709608137...
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

GIVEN d IS A DEONTIC `Redress party` `Redress step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ends fulfilled` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar date` d m y

§ `The dates`

-- s 2 table item 1 (column 3) and s 193(1)(a): the scheme runs from 1 July 2018 to the end of 1 July 2028.
#ASSERT `the scheme start day` EQUALS `on` 1 7 2018
#ASSERT `the scheme sunset day` EQUALS `on` 1 7 2028
-- A period of 6 months starting on 15 March ends on 14 September; starting on 31 August, at the end of February.
#ASSERT `the last day of the` 6 `month period starting on` (`on` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 14 9 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the` 6 `month period starting on` (`on` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of the` 6 `month period starting on` (`on` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 31 8 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the` 2 `month period starting on` (`on` 31 12 2026) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
-- Months back, across a year.
#ASSERT `the same day` (0 MINUS 4) `months on from` (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `on` 1 9 2026
#ASSERT `the same day` (0 MINUS 12) `months on from` (`on` 1 7 2028) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2027
-- Turning 18; a 29 February birthday (fork F8).
#ASSERT `the day I turn 18` (`on` 30 6 2010) EQUALS `on` 30 6 2028
#ASSERT `the day I turn 18` (`on` 29 2 2008) EQUALS `on` 1 3 2026
-- Whole years: the day before the anniversary, the anniversary.
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`on` 15 3 2016) `to` (`on` 14 3 2018) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`on` 15 3 2016) `to` (`on` 15 3 2018) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`on` 29 2 2008) `to` (`on` 28 2 2009) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`on` 29 2 2008) `to` (`on` 1 3 2009) EQUALS 1

§ `Can I apply`

-- An adult, in the ordinary course.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can apply to the Operator (s 19)`
-- The last ordinary day, and the first day of the last 12 months (s 20(1)(e)).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 30 6 2027) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can apply to the Operator (s 19)`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2027) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the application would be made in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day, and the Operator has not determined exceptional circumstances (s 20(1)(e), (2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2027) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the application falls in the last 12 months before the scheme sunset day, but the Operator has determined there are exceptional circumstances (s 20(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 30 6 2028) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the application would be made in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day, and the Operator has not determined exceptional circumstances (s 20(1)(e), (2))`
-- The sunset day itself is not "in the period of 12 months before" it (fork F1, finding 3).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2028) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can apply to the Operator (s 19)`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 2 7 2028) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the scheme has ended; the Act ceased to have effect at the end of the scheme sunset day (s 193(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 30 6 2018) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the day is before the scheme start day, 1 July 2018`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2018) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can apply to the Operator (s 19)`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 1 1970) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I have already made an application; only one withdrawn before it was decided does not count (ss 20(1)(a), 22(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 1 1970) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a security notice is in force in relation to me (s 20(1)(b))`
-- Children: born 30 June 2010 turns 18 on 30 June 2028, before the sunset day; born 1 July 2010 turns 18 on it.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 30 6 2010) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as a child: the Operator must deal with my application under the special process for child applicants and cannot decide it before I turn 18 (s 21; Rules s 15)`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 7 2010) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am a child who will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (s 20(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2027) (`on` 30 6 2010) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the application would be made in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day, and the Operator has not determined exceptional circumstances (s 20(1)(e), (2))`
-- The last day to apply.
#ASSERT `What is my last day to apply for redress question` (`on` 1 1 1970) EQUALS `my last day to apply, without needing the Operator to find exceptional circumstances, is` (`on` 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `What is my last day to apply for redress question` (`on` 30 6 2010) EQUALS `my last day to apply, without needing the Operator to find exceptional circumstances, is` (`on` 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `What is my last day to apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2010) EQUALS `only the scheme sunset day itself, 1 July 2028: before it I am a child who will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (s 20(1)(c)); on it I am 18, and on the literal reading the 12-month bar does not reach it (s 20(1)(e), fork F1), though the Act ceases at the end of that day (s 193(1))`
#ASSERT `What is my last day to apply for redress question` (`on` 2 7 2010) EQUALS `none: I will still be a child when the scheme ends, so I cannot apply as a child (s 20(1)(c)), and the Act ceases before I turn 18 (s 193(1))`
-- The two apply questions agree for a person born 1 July 2010 (fork F1): only the sunset day itself is open.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2028) (`on` 1 7 2010) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I can apply to the Operator (s 19)`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 30 6 2028) (`on` 1 7 2010) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I am a child who will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (s 20(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for redress question` (`on` 1 7 2028) (`on` 2 7 2010) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I am a child who will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (s 20(1)(c))`

§ `Scope and eligibility`

-- Born 10 May 1960: a child until 9 May 1978.
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 10 5 1960) (`on` 9 5 1978) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 10 5 1960) (`on` 10 5 1978) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not within the scope: I was not a child when it occurred (s 14(1)(a))`
-- The scheme start day: 30 June 2018 is before it, 1 July 2018 is not.
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 2005) (`on` 30 6 2018) `inside a Territory` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 2005) (`on` 1 7 2018) `inside a Territory` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not within the scope: it occurred on or after the scheme start day, 1 July 2018 (s 14(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `outside Australia` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`
-- A non-participating State: s 61.
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a State that is not a participating State` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `within the scope through s 61: it occurred in a non-participating State, but a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible; it counts if I am otherwise eligible (s 61(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a State that is not a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not within the scope: it occurred in a State that is not a participating State, and no Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible (ss 14(1)(b), 61)`
-- Rules s 6: abuse by a child without physical contact or penetration; the same without contact by an adult is in scope.
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not within the scope: it was sexual abuse by a child that did not involve physical contact with me or penetration of me (Rules s 6)`
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`

-- Eligibility (s 13). Base case: every condition met.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` FALSE (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a participating institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `no participating institution and no such listed institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `an institution listed for a participating jurisdiction under s 164A, 164B or 164C, and a participating jurisdiction is an eligible funding jurisdiction for it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a citizen or permanent resident: not eligible, unless a child migrant under Rules s 4B.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1945) (`on` 1 1 1955) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1945) (`on` 1 1 1955) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1945) (`on` 1 1 1955) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The s 61 route needs the citizenship condition in s 13(1)(e) (s 61(1)(a)); a child migrant without it is not eligible.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a State that is not a participating State` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1945) (`on` 1 1 1955) `inside a State that is not a participating State` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 1965) (`on` 1 1 1975) `inside a State that is not a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Abuse after the start day: out of scope, so not eligible.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for redress question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2005) (`on` 1 7 2018) `inside a participating State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a participating institution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Responsibility (s 15; Rules ss 11, 12).
#ASSERT `Is the institution responsible for my abuse question` `solely or primarily responsible for the abuser having contact with me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `responsible: primarily responsible (s 15(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Is the institution responsible for my abuse question` `approximately equally responsible with one or more other institutions, and no institution is primarily responsible` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `responsible: equally responsible (s 15(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Is the institution responsible for my abuse question` `neither` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible (s 15(1))`
#ASSERT `Is the institution responsible for my abuse question` `solely or primarily responsible for the abuser having contact with me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not responsible: a court ordered it to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse (Rules s 11)`
#ASSERT `Is the institution responsible for my abuse question` `approximately equally responsible with one or more other institutions, and no institution is primarily responsible` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not responsible: it is a government authority whose only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12)`

§ `After I apply`

-- s 24(4): a notice dated 2 March 2026: 4 weeks end on 29 March, 8 weeks on 26 April.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest my time to give information can end question` (`on` 2 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `on` 29 3 2026
#ASSERT `What is the earliest my time to give information can end question` (`on` 2 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `on` 26 4 2026

-- s 29 and Rules s 15(3): born 1 January 2009, applied 1 March 2026, turns 18 on 1 January 2027.
#ASSERT `What must the Operator do with my application question` FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 1970) (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS `not required to decide it: my application is not valid (s 19(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `What must the Operator do with my application question` TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 1 1970) (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS `not yet: I have not given information the Operator asked for within the production period; it need not decide until I do (s 26(1))`
#ASSERT `What must the Operator do with my application question` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 31 12 2026) TRUE EQUALS `not yet: I applied as a child; the Operator must not decide before I turn 18, and must decide as soon as practicable after (s 21; Rules s 15(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `What must the Operator do with my application question` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 1 2027) TRUE EQUALS `must approve my application and give me a written offer of redress (ss 29(2), 39)`
#ASSERT `What must the Operator do with my application question` TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 1970) (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `must decide not to approve my application (s 29(3)); I may apply for review (s 73)`

-- Rules s 15(2), the regulative rule: applied 1 March 2026, turns 18 on 1 January 2027; the window runs from 1 July
-- 2026 (day 122) to 1 October 2026 (day 214). A notice on day 121 does not count.
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me my notice before I turn 18` 122 214) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice before I turn 18` 122) 122)))
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me my notice before I turn 18` 122 214) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice before I turn 18` 214) 214)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me my notice before I turn 18` 122 214) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice before I turn 18` 121) 121), (WAITUNTIL 215)))))
-- expect: BREACH by the Operator (no notice in the window from 6 months to 3 months before I turn 18)
#TRACE `Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me my notice before I turn 18` 122 214 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Operator` DOES `give me the notice before I turn 18` 121 AT 121
    (WAITUNTIL 215)

#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 7 2026) (`on` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `given in time`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 10 2026) (`on` 2 10 2026) EQUALS `given in time`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 30 6 2026) (`on` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `not yet due: the Operator has until 3 months before I turn 18`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 30 6 2026) (`on` 2 10 2026) EQUALS `late: no notice in the window from 6 months to 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `not yet due: the Operator has until 3 months before I turn 18`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 2 10 2026) EQUALS `late: no notice in the window from 6 months to 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
-- Applied 1 September 2026, exactly 4 months before turning 18: the notice is required; 2 September: it is not.
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 1 9 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 2 10 2026) EQUALS `late: no notice in the window from 6 months to 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 2009) (`on` 2 9 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 2 10 2026) EQUALS `no notice is required: I applied less than 4 months before turning 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
#ASSERT `Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` (`on` 1 1 1970) (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) (`on` 2 10 2026) EQUALS `no notice is required: I was not a child when I applied`

§ `How much I get`

-- s 30, one responsible institution. No earlier payment, no advance: the maximum amount.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 80000 FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2021) FALSE EQUALS 80000
-- Step 1: the maximum is capped at $150,000; $150,000 itself is not reduced.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 200000 FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2021) FALSE EQUALS 150000
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 150000 FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2021) FALSE EQUALS 150000
-- s 30(5): an advance payment of $10,000 is taken off; never below nil.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 80000 FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2021) TRUE EQUALS 70000
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 8000 FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2021) TRUE EQUALS 0
-- Earlier payment of $20,000 on 15 March 2016; applied 15 March 2018 (n = 2), decided 20 March 2019 (n = 3).
-- Institution's share: 100000 - 21161.80 = 78838.20. Commonwealth's share: (100000 - 20767.22) - 78838.20 = 394.58.
-- Redress payment: 78838.20 + 394.58 = 79232.78.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 100000 TRUE 20000 (`on` 15 3 2016) (`on` 15 3 2018) (`on` 20 3 2019) FALSE EQUALS 79232.78
-- Decided two years later (n = 5 at the determination): the Commonwealth bears the extra years; still 79232.78.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 100000 TRUE 20000 (`on` 15 3 2016) (`on` 15 3 2018) (`on` 20 3 2021) FALSE EQUALS 79232.78
-- Applied one day before the second anniversary (n = 1): 100000 - 20380 = 79620.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 100000 TRUE 20000 (`on` 15 3 2016) (`on` 14 3 2018) (`on` 20 3 2019) FALSE EQUALS 79620
-- With the advance payment too: 79232.78 - 10000 = 69232.78.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 100000 TRUE 20000 (`on` 15 3 2016) (`on` 15 3 2018) (`on` 20 3 2019) TRUE EQUALS 69232.78
-- Applied and decided the day of the payment (n = 0): 100000 - 20000.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 100000 TRUE 20000 (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS 80000
-- An earlier payment larger than the maximum: nil.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 100000 TRUE 120000 (`on` 1 1 2019) (`on` 1 3 2019) (`on` 1 6 2019) FALSE EQUALS 0
-- The institution's share is nil at the determination (20500 - 20767.22) but 120 at the application (20500 - 20380):
-- the Commonwealth bears the 120, and the payment is 120.
#ASSERT `How much redress payment will I get question` 20500 TRUE 20000 (`on` 1 1 2018) (`on` 2 1 2019) (`on` 2 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `s 30(3) -- the institutions' total share` (LIST (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 20500, `its relevant prior payments` IS (LIST (`Relevant prior payment` WITH `original amount` IS 20000, `paid to me on` IS (`on` 1 1 2018))))) `counted to` (`on` 2 1 2020) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 30(4) -- the Commonwealth's share` (LIST (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 20500, `its relevant prior payments` IS (LIST (`Relevant prior payment` WITH `original amount` IS 20000, `paid to me on` IS (`on` 1 1 2018))))) (`on` 2 1 2019) (`on` 2 1 2020) EQUALS 120
-- The steps on their own: n = 3 gives 21161.80 (21161.79718 rounded up to the cent).
#ASSERT `s 30(2) step 5 -- the reduction amount for` (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 100000, `its relevant prior payments` IS (LIST (`Relevant prior payment` WITH `original amount` IS 20000, `paid to me on` IS (`on` 15 3 2016)))) `counted to` (`on` 20 3 2019) EQUALS 21161.80
#ASSERT `s 30(4) -- the Commonwealth's share` (LIST (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 100000, `its relevant prior payments` IS (LIST (`Relevant prior payment` WITH `original amount` IS 20000, `paid to me on` IS (`on` 15 3 2016))))) (`on` 15 3 2018) (`on` 20 3 2019) EQUALS 394.58
-- Two equally responsible institutions, gross liability $50,000 each; one paid $5,000 on 1 July 2015; applied 1 July
-- 2018 (n = 3: 5290.45), decided 1 July 2019. Payment: 100000 - 5290.45 = 94709.55; with an advance, 84709.55.
#ASSERT `s 30(5) -- the amount of my redress payment` (LIST (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 50000, `its relevant prior payments` IS (LIST (`Relevant prior payment` WITH `original amount` IS 5000, `paid to me on` IS (`on` 1 7 2015)))), (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 50000, `its relevant prior payments` IS EMPTY)) (`on` 1 7 2018) (`on` 1 7 2019) 0 EQUALS 94709.55
#ASSERT `s 30(5) -- the amount of my redress payment` (LIST (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 50000, `its relevant prior payments` IS (LIST (`Relevant prior payment` WITH `original amount` IS 5000, `paid to me on` IS (`on` 1 7 2015)))), (`Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS 50000, `its relevant prior payments` IS EMPTY)) (`on` 1 7 2018) (`on` 1 7 2019) 10000 EQUALS 84709.55

-- Rules s 26: how much of an earlier payment counts.
