§ `If the applicant dies`

#ASSERT `What happens to the redress payment if the applicant dies question` `before the Operator decided the application` FALSE EQUALS `the application continues; if approved, the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 58, 60)`
#ASSERT `What happens to the redress payment if the applicant dies question` `after being given an offer, before accepting, declining or its withdrawal` FALSE EQUALS `the offer is withdrawn; the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 59(2), (3), 60)`
#ASSERT `What happens to the redress payment if the applicant dies question` `after being given an offer, before accepting, declining or its withdrawal` TRUE EQUALS `the offer is withdrawn; the review continues, and if it approves the application the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 59(2), (4), 60)`
#ASSERT `What happens to the redress payment if the applicant dies question` `after accepting the offer` FALSE EQUALS `the redress payment, or any unpaid instalments, is still paid, to an account the executor or administrator nominates if the applicant's own account can no longer be used (s 48(1D); Rules s 33(3))`
#ASSERT `What happens to the redress payment if the applicant dies question` `after declining the offer` FALSE EQUALS `nothing is payable: the offer was declined (s 45)`

